      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 1991, Emslie-Smith and Engel described a distinct form of idiopathic inflammatory myopathy they called \"necrotizing myopathy with pipestem capillaries, microvascular deposition of the complement membrane attack complex (MAC) and minimal cellular infiltration.\" We describe a patient with exercise-dependent painful myopathy related to a necrotizing myopathy with pipestem capillaries in whom mild cutaneous signs of dermatomyositis were detected 7 years after onset and who subsequently developed multiple cerebral infarcts."},
